All verified by inline gates (compile-clean + fresh-actor live particle counts); user visual review pending.

- **First-tick velocity spike clamp** — `BP_WaterBlobManager` position-delta velocity now passes through `ClampVectorSize(0..1500)` before injection, bounding the PrevPos=origin startup spike to one plausible-speed frame.
- **Tuning scalars opened as User parameters** — `SP_CharInteract` rebuilt (delete+recreate reset pattern) with 4 float module inputs (`AttractRadius`, `AttractStrength`, `ScatterVelThreshold`, `ScatterStrength`) created via the C++ `parameter_inputs` path (Module.* ParameterMapGet reads) and stack-linked to the pre-existing `User.*` floats via `set_niagara_module_input_user_parameter`. DI arrays auto-bound 3/3 as before. Values now: 400 / 120 / 250 / 2000.
  - **Float binding proven numerically**: temp `SP_FloatProbe` (kill when `Module.TestRadius` < 350, linked to `User.AttractRadius`) — component-level `set_niagara_variable_float("User.AttractRadius", 300)` collapsed 422 spawned → 1 live. The User-float → Module-input → GPU HLSL chain works per-component at runtime; scalars are live-tunable during PIE/editor review. Probe removed after the gate.
- **Parameter hygiene** — removed orphans `User.MeshList` (only consumer was the disabled mesh renderer) and `User.CharCount` (HLSL uses `Array.Length()`); exposed set is now exactly 7 (4 tuning floats + 3 char arrays). Note: the active mesh renderer's `meshes_binding` names `User.DropletMeshes`, which no longer exists — rendering comes from the renderer-local mesh array (Sphere, scale 0.2); binding is inert, cleanup optional.
- **Capsule measured per-character** — BP now feeds `CharCapsules` from `GetComponentByClass(CapsuleComponent)` → `GetScaledCapsuleRadius/HalfHeight` → `MakeVector(R, H, 0)`, with `SelectVector` falling back to `(42, 90, 0)` when the pawn has no capsule (cast bSuccess drives the select).
- **Tooling note** — `parameter_inputs` on `insert_niagara_scratch_pad_custom_hlsl_for_pin` is not exposed by the Python tool schema; route through `execute_batch` raw bridge params (same workaround as the MakeArray `[0]` pin).

Final gate: rebuilt BP manager + rebuilt SP compile clean; fresh spawn shows 211 live GPU particles; User param set inspected clean. Awaiting user visual review of attraction/scatter feel (scalars adjustable live via User parameters).

## 15. Visual-review round 1: scatter 60%, soft separation, BP-linked overlap range (2026-07-11)

User visual verdict on M2-b: feel is good; requested (a) scatter push at 60%, (b) droplets should not overlap *too much* (soft separation, partial overlap fine), (c) the overlap range exposed as a BP parameter linked to a Niagara User parameter.

- **Scatter 60%** — `User.ScatterStrength` 2000 → 1200 (value-only change, no recompile).
- **Soft separation without neighbor reads** — true particle-particle separation needs Particle Attribute Reader (C++ backlog, planned for M4 merge). Instead `SP_CharInteract` (rebuilt as `SP_CharInteract_1`, stack index 1) gives each particle a stable random personal-space distance: `Hold = 30 + Rand0(uid) * SeparationSpread`. Attraction only pulls while `Surface > Hold` (falloff renormalized to the Hold..AttractRadius band); inside the hold band an outward push up to `1.5 × AttractStrength` scaled by penetration creates layered equilibrium shells. A per-particle tangential offset (`normalize(-Dir + Tangent * (Rand1-0.5) * 0.6)`) breaks angular bunching. Escalation path if visual result is insufficient: PAR-based true separation.
- **New `User.SeparationSpread`** (float, default 120) — created via module-input link (5th tuning float; inputs now AttractRadius/AttractStrength/ScatterVelThreshold/ScatterStrength/SeparationSpread + 3 char arrays, DI auto-bound 3/3).
- **BP linkage** — `BP_WaterBlobManager` gains instance-editable `SeparationSpread` (category "WaterBlob Tuning", default 120); tick chain extended: ... → Set PrevPos → `SetNiagaraVariableFloat("User.SeparationSpread", var)`. Editing the actor's detail-panel value drives the GPU live.

Gates: Niagara compile clean (0 errors, GPU ready); BP compile clean, saved; fresh manager spawn 209 live particles; exposed param set = 8. Awaiting visual re-review.

