## 27. Main-droplet masked-dither spawn fade and Empty capsule safety (2026-07-12)

The main droplets now fade in through `ParticleColor.A` while preserving the existing masked material, spline spawn path, fixed-population controller, character attraction/scatter, and death-site Burst. The Empty-map capsule warning discovered during the runtime gate was also fixed without replacing the measured-capsule behavior used by real characters. Water, Ground/Snow, `NS_WaterBurst`, `NDC_WaterBlobBurst`, and the material asset were not edited.

### Masked-dither fade

- `NS_WaterBlob_V8` gained `User.SpawnFadeDuration` (float, default `0.35`).
- Particle Update gained one system scratch module, `SP_SpawnFade_0`, after the existing Color module and before Drag. Its HLSL uses a smoothstep-shaped age ramp and multiplies only the current particle alpha:

  `FadeT = saturate(Age / max(SpawnFadeDuration, 0.001))`

  `SpawnFade = FadeT * FadeT * (3 - 2 * FadeT)`

  `SpawnFadeColor = float4(Color.rgb, Color.a * SpawnFade)`

- The final Particle Update order is Particle State -> SP Char Interact -> SP Drift Bob -> Color -> SP Spawn Fade -> Drag -> Curl Noise Force -> Solve Forces and Velocity.
- `User.SpawnFadeDuration` is linked through the stack override to `Module.SpawnFadeDuration`; post-restart inspection found exactly one fade scratch script, one stack instance, and zero stale fade override/MapGet nodes.
- `M_WaterDroplet_MaskedDither` was intentionally left byte-identical. It already multiplies `ParticleColor.A` into OpacityMask, so the Niagara alpha ramp reaches the masked-dither cutout without a material edit.

Technical render proof used transient PIE overrides only: a `5.0` second duration captured immediately after reinitialize produced 21 blue-mask pixels, while a post-restart `0.001` second duration produced 5,218; the image difference contained 6,096 nonzero pixels. The asset and component defaults remained `0.35` after the probe. The final look at the default duration remains a user visual gate.

### Empty-map `Accessed None` fix without behavior regression

The warning was caused by the capsule-less `SpectatorPawn` in `/Game/Template/Empty`. The previous pure `Select Vector` was not a lazy guard: its measured-value input evaluated `GetScaledCapsuleRadius` and `GetScaledCapsuleHalfHeight` on the failed CapsuleComponent cast before the selector could choose `(42,90,0)`.

The final BP graph keeps both paths:

1. `Select Object` chooses the actual CapsuleComponent when the original cast succeeds, otherwise `/Script/Engine.Default__CapsuleComponent` as a valid getter source.
2. A safe cast feeds both scaled-capsule getters, so neither getter can dereference `None`.
3. The original cast-success boolean still drives `Select Vector`: real characters publish their measured radius/half-height; capsule-less pawns publish the existing `(42,90,0)` fallback.

This preserves character attraction/scatter sizing instead of replacing all pawns with a hard-coded capsule. A temporary fallback-component canary route was rejected after editor instability and was never promoted; the final manager has exactly the original `BlobFX` and `SpawnZone` components, and all WaterBlob canary assets were deleted.

