## 30. Burst source-velocity inheritance (2026-07-12)

Death-site fragments now inherit the dying droplet's NDC velocity while preserving the approved radial Burst. The existing NDC schema already contained `Position` and `Velocity`, so the Data Channel asset was not changed.

### Implementation

`NS_WaterBurst`:

- Added Vector User parameter `User.SourceVelocity`, default `(0,0,0)`.
- Added one system-owned Particle Spawn Scratch Pad, `SP_InheritSourceVelocity_0`, after the existing radial `AddVelocity` and before the downstream spawn assignment/output.
- The module writes `Particles.Velocity` through one stack-context expression: `PreviousVelocity + SourceVelocity`.
- `Module.SourceVelocity` is linked to `User.SourceVelocity` on the exact new module GUID. No second stock AddVelocity was added, avoiding alias and RapidIteration collisions.
- Zero input is exact behavior parity: the approved radial speed remains 250.

`BP_WaterBlobManager`:

- Added the pure NDC reader call `ReadVector("Velocity")` using the same Reader object and ForLoop Index already used by `ReadPosition("Position")`.
- The existing `SpawnSystemAtLocation` remains at the death position but now uses `bAutoActivate=false`.
- Its returned NiagaraComponent passes through `IsValid`/Branch because the preserved `bPreCullCheck=true` path may return null.
- On the valid path, `SetVariableVec3("User.SourceVelocity", ReadVector.ReturnValue)` executes before `Activate(bReset=true)`. This prevents a first-tick default-zero race.
- `bAutoDestroy=true`, `PoolingMethod=None`, and the existing replenish/NDC loop remain unchanged.

